Nodes: Graph

Purpose:
  Defines node types and ID conventions for the knowledge graph.

NodeTypes:
  PROMPT:
    Format: PROMPT-NNN
    Description: User input or AI prompt
  REQUIREMENT:
    Format: REQ-NNN
    Description: Business or technical requirement
  DECISION:
    Format: DEC-NNN
    Description: Architecture or technology decision
  TASK:
    Format: TASK-NNN or domain prefix (PAY-NNN)
    Description: Work item
  WORKFLOW:
    Format: WF-NNN
    Description: Workflow instance
  SKILL:
    Format: SKILL-NAME
    Description: Reusable knowledge package
  PROJECT:
    Format: PROJECT
    Description: Project node
  DOMAIN:
    Format: DOMAIN-NAME
    Description: Business domain
  MODULE:
    Format: MODULE-NAME
    Description: Code module
  COMPONENT:
    Format: COMPONENT-NAME
    Description: Code component
  CODE:
    Format: CODE-PREFIX-NAME
    Description: Source code file or function
  BDD:
    Format: BDD-TASK-NNN
    Description: BDD scenario
  TEST:
    Format: TEST-TASK-NNN
    Description: Test case
  SECURITY:
    Format: SEC-NNN
    Description: Security control or finding
  INFRA:
    Format: INFRA-NAME
    Description: Infrastructure component
  DEPLOYMENT:
    Format: DEPLOY-NNN
    Description: Deployment instance
  RUNTIME:
    Format: RUNTIME
    Description: Runtime state
  INCIDENT:
    Format: INC-YYYYMMDD-NNN
    Description: Production incident
  DOCUMENT:
    Format: DOC-NAME
    Description: Human-readable document

NodeRules:
  [ND1]  Every major object MUST be a node.
  [ND2]  Node IDs MUST be standardized and unique.
  [ND3]  Node IDs enable short references instead of long paths.
  [ND4]  Graph is index, not copy.

State: +
  